  "claim_map": [
    {
      "topic": "feed identity",
      "2024": "Main p. 3 section 2.1 and Table 2: homogenized powder, d80 97.9 micrometres; Cr 82340, Cu 59725, Ni 109194 ppm. K 875 ppm. Sludge supplier/site/batch not named.",
      "2026": "Main pp. 2–3 Tables 2–3: d80 97.9 micrometres; prose Cr 8.23%, Cu 5.97%, Ni 10.92%; K 785 ppm; Table 2 mixes oxide and elemental labels, Table 3 labels Si 435 ppm (2024 Table 2 labels Sr 435). SI S1 feed XRD; S2 distribution. Sludge supplier/site/batch not named.",
      "disposition": "Matching d80, rounded major metals, and several trace values do not establish one physical batch or independent replication. Do not relabel Si as Sr or reconcile K by assumption."
    },
    {
      "topic": "reagent and organism",
      "2024": "Main p. 3: filtered steel-company pickling liquor, 255.3 g/L iron ions and 2.5 g/L H+; Table 3S declared but missing. No microorganism in this leaching experiment.",
      "2026": "Main pp. 2–4 and SI S3: A. ferrooxidans from Soil and Water Research Institute, Karaj, no strain identifier; 100 mL cultures with 10% inoculum, initial pH 1.8, 34 C/140 rpm for one week; liquor pH 1.2, ORP 650 mV, Fe3+ 9 g/L; centrifuged 5000 rpm for 15 min before leaching. Sulfur/ferrous medium and initial sulfuric acid are contributors. Medium prints 44.22 g/L Fe2SO4·7H2O and elsewhere 44.7 g/L FeSO4·7H2O.",
      "disposition": "Distinct chemical reagents. Neither cells in direct sludge contact nor a unique metabolite advantage is established by the 2026 cell-removal protocol. Chemistry-matched acid/ferric control explicitly proposed as future work p. 11."
    },
    {
      "topic": "assay and replication",
      "2024": "Main pp. 3–6: 100 mL liquor in 250 mL three-neck flask, bath/reflux, magnetic stirring; ICP-OES at 10,20,30,60,120 min and temperature series at 0.5,1,2,4,8,12,20,30,60,120 min. Visible error bars, but inspected main does not define n/error statistic.",
      "2026": "Main pp. 3–4 Table 4 and SI S4: 100 mL cell-removed reagent, 250 mL three-neck flask, 37 kHz/150 W ultrasonic bath, one-factor-at-a-time; experiments performed three times with means/SD. Fig. 1 compares ultrasound/no ultrasound at ambient,400 rpm,10 g/L. Table 4 lists six solids levels including 25 g/L; Fig. 3 displays five, without 25.",
      "disposition": "Separate arms, times and preparation stages. No raw replicate table or full cumulative-sampling balance acquired. Do not infer biological replicates or culture purity."
    },
    {
      "topic": "repeated 120-minute values",
      "2024": "Abstract p. 1; results pp. 5–6; conclusion p. 9: Cr 92.33%, Cu 89.49%, Ni 89.59% at 120 min,25 C,300 rpm,10 g/L. Fig. 2 caption300 rpm. Fig. 3 temperature-series caption400 rpm.",
      "2026": "SI Table S1 wastewater row cites reference [3] Kordloo 2024 and gives Ni 89.59%,Cu 89.49%,Cr 92.33%,120 min,25 C,300 rpm,10 g/L. Main p. 4 ultrasound prose repeats exact triple, near references 59/60 to other ultrasound papers. Main pp. 6–7 rounds triple to Cr 92.3%,Cu 89.5%,Ni 89.6% under400 rpm/ambient.",
